      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَيِّلُ اللَّحْمِ</span></b>  A man <i>having much flesh:</i> (T, O, *
K:) some pronounce it with <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ء</span>, (T, O,) saying
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَيأَل</span>, (T,) or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَئِل</span>; (O;) both mentioned before
[in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فأل</span>]. (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَيِّلُ الرَّأْىِ</span>: see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فِيلٌ</span>,
latter half.

